<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>The Track of CLS token in Sampled Tasks</h3>

<figure id="A1.F26" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.07787v1/appendix_cls.png" id="A1.F26.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:286/461;" width="286" height="461" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 26: </span>The effective rank of each component of cls token in ViT during continual learning. The order of components starts from embedding layers, 12 ViT blocks, and classification head. The sampled tasks are task 1 (blue), task 51 (orange), task 101 (green), task 151 (red), and task 201 (purple).</figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>The Fraction of Active/Dead Units in ViT</h3>

<figure id="A1.F27" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.07787v1/faufdu.png" id="A1.F27.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:238/276;" width="238" height="276" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 27: </span>The FAU (blue) and FDU (orange) in activation function of FFN in ViT’s 12 blocks. The significant decrease of FAU and the rise of FDU demonstrate the loss of adaptability in FFN module.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Performance of Plasticity Loss mitigating Method: CReLU</h3>

<figure id="A2.F28" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2603.07787v1/crelu_accuracies_moving_average.svg" id="A2.F28.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:333/153;" width="333" height="153"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 28: </span>The accuracy curves of Upper bound (red), vanilla ViT (brown), and ViT with CReLU (orange) on first 25 tasks of stream. The AAT of CReLU is 0.617, which is less than vanilla ViT (0.638) and Upper bound (0.732), indicating the worse performance of CReLU. Moreover, the cost of CReLU is double than other approaches.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>The Hyperparameter Adjustment Results</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The details of the entire hyperparameters tuning of ARROW including fixed values and decay schedule. Here, <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> annotates with <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> of ARROW. <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a1e-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a1e-1</annotation></semantics></math> represents the value of <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times\mathrm{e}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times\mathrm{e}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w20</annotation></semantics></math> represents the window size of the gradient buffer is 20; <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b0.9</annotation></semantics></math> means the value of <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is 0.9. The followed ’rms’ means the employment of RMS-like warm-up mode, whereas the SGD is used without ’rms’. ’Trac’ represent the adaptive learning rate is introduced to ARROW. If the decay schedule is introduced for <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> per task, we can see symbol of ’pertask’.</p>
</div>
